# Chapter One — the Harbour.
# Question: who was at the tower at midnight, and why?
# Red herring: Otto, seen on the green at midnight, resolving warmly.

@node ch1_dock_open
  The harbour is the only part of Prismbrook that has not noticed it is gray,
  because the harbour was never the colourful bit.
  Even so, the sea has gone the shade of a dropped coin, and two women on the
  wall are looking at it and not saying anything at all.

@node otto_intro
  [if flag ch1.met_otto == 0]
  OTTO(worried): Cold morning, detective. Colder without the blue, if you ask
  me.
  YOU:
    * (kind) Everyone misses it, Mr. Brine.  -> otto_warm
    * (dry) The fish seem to be coping.  -> otto_chuckle
    * (curious) You were up on Tower Green last night.  -> otto_accused
  [else]
  goto otto_after
  [end]

@node otto_warm
  OTTO(moved): ...Aye. Well. Ask your questions.
  trust otto 1
  goto otto_midnight

@node otto_chuckle
  OTTO(laughing): The fish have never once given a fig about anything. Ask
  your questions.
  goto otto_midnight

@node otto_accused
  OTTO(shifty): Who says that.
  OTTO(shifty): No. Do not tell me. I know who says that. Everybody says that.
  goto otto_midnight

@node otto_midnight
  set ch1.met_otto = 1
  OTTO(worried): You will have heard I was on the green after midnight. I
  was. I have been every night this week.
  grant clue.midnight_figure
  YOU:
    * (kind) You do not have to tell me why.  -> otto_free
    * (curious) Doing what, at midnight, on the green?  -> otto_why
    * (dry) A man could get himself talked about.  -> otto_why

@node otto_free
  OTTO(moved): I know. That is why I am going to.
  trust otto 1
  goto otto_why

@node otto_why
  OTTO(sad): There is a bird up that tower that has not eaten properly in a
  week, because this town decided he was a thief and this town stopped
  putting things out.
  grant clue.pip_hungry
  OTTO: So I take a pail up. Fish heads, mostly. He does not come down while
  I am there. He waits until I have gone off the green.
  grant clue.fish_pail
  YOU:
    * (kind) That is a decent thing to do for a suspect.  -> otto_decent
    * (curious) Why not just tell people?  -> otto_tell
    * (dry) Feeding the accused. Very irregular.  -> otto_decent

@node otto_decent
  OTTO(shifty): It is a pail of heads. Do not make a speech of it.
  OTTO(moved): Nobody should go hungry. Not even a thief. Especially not a
  thief who is nine ounces.
  trust otto 1
  goto otto_task

@node otto_tell
  OTTO(worried): And have them laugh? Or worse, have them stop me?
  goto otto_task

@node otto_task
  OTTO: Right. If you want the whole of my night you will have to earn it,
  and I have got crates to order before the ice goes.
  OTTO(happy): Five crates, no marks on them, one balance. Sort me those and
  I will give you the lot, times and all.
  start_puzzle weights_sorting
  OTTO(moved): Lightest to heaviest and not a scale in sight. You have a head
  on you.
  OTTO: I went up at half eleven. I was off the green before one. I saw
  nobody go in and nobody come out, and I would have.
  set ch1.otto_done = 1
  trust otto 1

@node otto_after
  [if flag ch1.otto_done == 1]
  OTTO: Ask Tansy. She is nine and she watches everything and nobody has
  thought to ask her a single question.
  [else]
  OTTO(worried): Come back when you have a minute for the crates.
  goto otto_task
  [end]

@node tansy_intro
  [if flag ch1.met_tansy == 0]
  TANSY(happy): Are you the detective? You do not look like one.
  YOU:
    * (kind) What is a detective supposed to look like?  -> tansy_look
    * (dry) Neither do you, and yet here we are.  -> tansy_look
    * (curious) I hear you are the one who watches the tower.  -> tansy_watch
  [else]
  goto tansy_after
  [end]

@node tansy_look
  TANSY(laughing): Taller. And with a big coat that goes out at the bottom
  when you turn round fast.
  TANSY: I have thought about it a lot.
  trust tansy 1
  goto tansy_watch

@node tansy_watch
  set ch1.met_tansy = 1
  TANSY(worried): Everyone says Pip took the shiny thing. Everyone is wrong.
  YOU:
    * (curious) Tell me what you saw.  -> tansy_saw_it
    * (kind) You sound very sure. Why?  -> tansy_sure
    * (dry) Everyone is usually wrong. Go on.  -> tansy_saw_it

@node tansy_sure
  TANSY(sad): Because he is not being a thief. He is being sad. They look
  completely different and grown-ups cannot tell.
  TANSY: He is not bad. He is just sad.
  trust tansy 1
  goto tansy_saw_it

@node tansy_saw_it
  TANSY: I was on the wall late because of the crabs. Crabs are late.
  TANSY(worried): He came down at the fish stall and then he went up at the
  tower and then he came down again and then he went up again. Loads of times.
  YOU:
    * (curious) Like he was going back and forth on purpose?  -> tansy_purpose
    * (kind) That sounds tiring, for a bird.  -> tansy_purpose
    * (dry) Busy night for a master criminal.  -> tansy_purpose

@node tansy_purpose
  TANSY(happy): Like when you pull someone's sleeve. Exactly like that.
  TANSY: If you want the whole of it you have to play shells with me. That is
  the rule. It has always been the rule.
  start_puzzle shell_memory
  TANSY(laughing): You are quite good at that for a grown-up.
  TANSY(sad): He was not carrying anything. Not once. Not going up and not
  coming down. I looked, because I wanted him not to be.
  set ch1.tansy_done = 1
  trust tansy 1

@node tansy_after
  [if flag ch1.tansy_done == 1]
  TANSY(happy): Captain Sorge writes down every single boat. Every one. She
  is worse than me.
  [else]
  TANSY: Shells first. Rules are rules.
  goto tansy_purpose
  [end]

@node maribel_intro
  [if flag ch1.met_maribel == 0]
  MARIBEL(neutral): You will be wanting the log.
  YOU:
    * (curious) I will be wanting the log.  -> maribel_log
    * (kind) I will be wanting whatever you can spare, Captain.  -> maribel_spare
    * (dry) Am I that obvious?  -> maribel_obvious
  [else]
  goto maribel_after
  [end]

@node maribel_obvious
  MARIBEL(laughing): You are a coat with a notebook in it. Yes.
  goto maribel_log

@node maribel_spare
  MARIBEL(moved): ...That is a kinder way of asking than I am used to.
  trust maribel 1
  goto maribel_log

@node maribel_log
  set ch1.met_maribel = 1
  MARIBEL: I write every crossing. Time out, time in, to the minute. Forty
  years of it, and my mother's before.
  MARIBEL(shifty): It is not sentiment. It is a log.
  YOU:
    * (kind) It is a little bit sentiment.  -> maribel_sentiment
    * (curious) Then you will know who was moving after midnight.  -> maribel_task
    * (dry) Forty years of nothing happening, minuted.  -> maribel_task

@node maribel_sentiment
  MARIBEL(moved): ...It is a little bit sentiment. My mother's hand is in the
  front of it and mine is in the back and I do not intend to explain that
  further.
  trust maribel 1
  goto maribel_task

@node maribel_task
  MARIBEL: I will read you the small hours. First, the ferry is loose and I
  will not have her loose.
  MARIBEL: Run me a line from the bollard to the ferry and take in every
  cleat on the way. A rope that skips a cleat is a rope that lets go.
  start_puzzle rope_knot
  MARIBEL(happy): Hm. Seaman's hands on a paper-pusher.
  MARIBEL: Small hours, then. Nothing crossed. Nothing at all until the milk
  boat at four.
  MARIBEL(worried): But I was on deck. And I will tell you what I saw on the
  green, because you asked properly.
  MARIBEL: A lamp going up the outside stair a little after midnight, and no
  lamp coming down. I assumed it was Iris. It is always Iris.
  set ch1.maribel_done = 1
  trust maribel 1

@node maribel_after
  [if flag ch1.maribel_done == 1]
  MARIBEL: A lamp that goes up and does not come down is a lamp that is still
  up there, detective. Draw your own conclusion. I have drawn mine twice.
  [else]
  MARIBEL: The rope first.
  goto maribel_task
  [end]
